[SPEAKER_01]: There's always introduction to the mind, always there.

32
00:04:12,211 --> 00:04:31,120
[SPEAKER_01]: So I think this is not something that it is only given to some people, it's always given, but I think the special kind of what we call the peace instruction or whatever, when the time is right, and I think master says a few things and then you somehow

33
00:04:32,341 --> 00:04:34,206
[SPEAKER_01]: actualize or get it.

34
00:04:34,627 --> 00:04:39,178
[SPEAKER_01]: There are some stories again with the Patrul Rinpoche, connected with Patrul Rinpoche.

35
00:04:40,142 --> 00:04:49,190
[SPEAKER_01]: that some incidents that Patrul Rinpoche's teacher, he sort of hit him on the head and call him a mad dog and then that sort of wake him up.

36
00:04:51,652 --> 00:04:55,315
[SPEAKER_01]: Not always hitting, some other cases no hitting also.

37
00:04:57,397 --> 00:05:06,225
[SPEAKER_01]: Patrul Rinpoche and his student Nyoshulungtok, sitting in the meadow of Dzogchen, near this snow mountain.

38
00:05:07,545 --> 00:05:13,506
[SPEAKER_01]: And Patrul Rinpoche, I think it must be in the evening, he said, can you see the stars in the sky?

39
00:05:14,466 --> 00:05:15,567
[SPEAKER_01]: Then his students, yes.

40
00:05:17,307 --> 00:05:20,008
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you hear the dogs barking in the village?

41
00:05:20,968 --> 00:05:21,988
[SPEAKER_01]: Students says yes.

42
00:05:23,068 --> 00:05:24,668
[SPEAKER_01]: So what is the nature of your mind?

43
00:05:26,109 --> 00:05:27,649
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's all it takes.

44
00:05:29,509 --> 00:05:32,090
[SPEAKER_01]: So I think a lot of maturation, maturation.

45
00:05:33,842 --> 00:05:37,104
[SPEAKER_01]: preparation, preparation, maturation, I think.

46
00:05:37,984 --> 00:05:43,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Then we will kind of actualize or realize this kind of thing.

47
00:05:44,048 --> 00:05:49,271
[SPEAKER_01]: So speaking too much I think doesn't really make much difference.

48
00:05:49,311 --> 00:05:52,652
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like maybe I'm telling you how to ride a bicycle.

49
00:05:52,672 --> 00:05:57,655
[SPEAKER_01]: So here in the poem that Khyentse Rinpoche wrote,

50
00:06:07,857 --> 00:06:14,701
[SPEAKER_01]: So here I will ask Sean to translate so if I make a mistake I can blame him.

51
00:06:32,648 --> 00:06:37,469
[SPEAKER_01]: When we think of the human experience, we are a composite of body, mind and speech running between the two.

52
00:06:58,218 --> 00:07:03,419
[SPEAKER_00]: From within these three, body, speech and mind, mind is the most important.

53
00:07:04,419 --> 00:07:10,781
[SPEAKER_00]: And with regard to subduing of the mind or the subjugation of the unruly emotions and thoughts etc.

54
00:07:10,821 --> 00:07:15,242
[SPEAKER_00]: that run wild in our mind, the Buddha gave numerous teachings.

55
00:07:21,797 --> 00:07:23,479
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't want to do it, don't do it.

56
00:07:23,539 --> 00:07:24,840
[SPEAKER_01]: If you want to do it, don't do it.

57
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:27,042
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't want to do it, don't do it.

58
00:07:27,102 --> 00:07:28,764
[SPEAKER_01]: If you want to do it, don't do it.

59
00:07:28,804 --> 00:07:30,245
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't want to do it, don't do it.

60
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:56,953
[SPEAKER_00]: So as I mentioned, the Buddha gave innumerable teachings, all of which have the sole purpose of subduing or subjugating the unruly mind.

61
00:07:58,852 --> 00:08:13,341
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, if one were to kind of put all of these together or to combine all of these in a very simple way, then one shouldn't look outside of oneself for a method or a means, independence upon which one can subdue the mind.

62
00:08:13,421 --> 00:08:15,863
[SPEAKER_00]: Rather, one should look within oneself.

63
00:08:16,884 --> 00:08:26,470
[SPEAKER_00]: So here then, the first line of the poem reads, when mind is watching mind, as such, rather than looking outside of oneself, one must choose to look within.

64
00:08:27,694 --> 00:08:34,619
[SPEAKER_00]: One will find then that mind and the one who is supposedly watching mind are not separate, rather they are one and the same.

65
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:38,622
[SPEAKER_01]: So when one kind of looks within,

66
00:08:58,937 --> 00:09:01,918
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, looking at the mind, there is nothing to see.

67
00:09:03,078 --> 00:09:03,958
[SPEAKER_00]: It is vividly clear.

68
00:09:05,118 --> 00:09:13,500
[SPEAKER_00]: So when one tries to look at mind, there is nothing, there is no color, neither is there a shape upon which to focus.

69
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:17,121
[SPEAKER_00]: Rather, when mind is watching mind, there is nothing to see.

70
00:09:18,121 --> 00:09:21,942
[SPEAKER_00]: But it isn't that there is something obscured or that there is something hidden away.

71
00:09:22,122 --> 00:09:26,183
[SPEAKER_00]: Rather, the nature of one's mind is something that is vividly clear.

72
00:09:27,938 --> 00:09:35,582
[SPEAKER_01]: In Tibetan, there is a saying that if you don't know how to be a good person, you can't be a good person.

73
00:09:49,053 --> 00:09:49,954
[SPEAKER_00]: So how to do that?

74
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:56,362
[SPEAKER_00]: How to then kind of rest within the nature of mind and see then this natural luminosity of mind?

75
00:09:57,163 --> 00:10:03,410
[SPEAKER_00]: We were advised then in the third line that one should rest naturally and how should that rest occur?

76
00:10:03,971 --> 00:10:05,312
[SPEAKER_00]: It should be uncontrived.

77
00:10:05,953 --> 00:10:14,237
[SPEAKER_00]: Here then, one shouldn't confuse oneself, nor should one kind of stir up the mind, but rather one should simply allow things to settle.

78
00:10:14,797 --> 00:10:23,601
[SPEAKER_00]: One shouldn't give rise to an emotion, neither should one give rise to a chain of thoughts, but rather remain without contriving the mind, free and at ease.

79
00:10:36,337 --> 00:10:45,339
[SPEAKER_00]: As such, when one allows thought to rest naturally and everything becomes still, becomes quiet then, one should be alert.

80
00:10:46,240 --> 00:11:03,184
[SPEAKER_00]: If distraction occurs, if one becomes distracted, if thought arises that would ruin one's meditation, one should recognize that and simply let it go and remain, as is written here, resting naturally and without distraction.

81
00:11:05,782 --> 00:11:11,061
[SPEAKER_01]: So I think when we do this kind of looking into your mind,

82
00:11:12,118 --> 00:11:17,781
[SPEAKER_01]: I think first thing I think we have to forget about all the intellectual understanding of what is mind.

83
00:11:18,722 --> 00:11:22,003
[SPEAKER_01]: Or philosophical ideas that we have put into our brain.

84
00:11:22,544 --> 00:11:27,006
[SPEAKER_01]: Or even scientific ideas of how the brain and all the cells work.

85
00:11:27,706 --> 00:11:33,970
[SPEAKER_01]: So because this thing, this intellectual understanding can affect the actual understanding of the mind, I think.

86
00:11:34,570 --> 00:11:39,953
[SPEAKER_01]: So therefore you should be a little bit like a young child or forget all these things.

87
00:11:41,642 --> 00:11:50,468
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't realize, but I was told by Chabji Thimken Rinpoche to get the mind instruction from his son, his 16th Karmapa.

88
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:55,472
[SPEAKER_01]: And I was only about seven years old, or seven or six years old.

89
00:11:56,473 --> 00:12:04,439
[SPEAKER_01]: And they would sit next to each other, and then Karmapa would tell me, okay, tomorrow you have to tell me what your minds look like.

90
00:12:05,619 --> 00:12:10,403
[SPEAKER_01]: Then I go and think all night, oh, my mind is like a mountain.

91
00:12:11,733 --> 00:12:13,575
[SPEAKER_01]: I go back and I report next day.

92
00:12:14,155 --> 00:12:15,756
[SPEAKER_01]: And both of them, ah, ha, ha, ha.

93
00:12:19,259 --> 00:12:23,262
[SPEAKER_01]: So, they're sort of waiting for my next reply.

94
00:12:24,463 --> 00:12:26,465
[SPEAKER_01]: Every time I come with very strange ideas.

95
00:12:28,306 --> 00:12:32,149
[SPEAKER_01]: So I think, like child's mind, we don't have so much concept.

96
00:12:33,110 --> 00:12:34,511
[SPEAKER_01]: Sort of just pure.

97
00:12:35,391 --> 00:12:36,492
[SPEAKER_01]: Then look, look back.

98
00:12:42,490 --> 00:12:54,320
[SPEAKER_01]: SHARVE SHILA, SHARVE SHILA MATIPAR, CHUNG NA SHARGYEN THEGALE, NAMDOG CHOK SHARWA THI NAMDOG THI, THA THEN GOM CHENG NAMDOG THANGWA SHARWA THA, THEN NGON ZIN THUG WUG WUG YORIS.

99
00:12:58,377 --> 00:13:05,201
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever thought occurs from that state, without stopping or analyzing, watch its very nature.

100
00:13:06,161 --> 00:13:09,003
[SPEAKER_00]: Its arising doesn't obscure the absolute nature.

101
00:13:09,863 --> 00:13:12,824
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever occurs, relax right there.

102
00:13:14,145 --> 00:13:30,430
[SPEAKER_00]: Here then, when we are trying to remain within the natural state, the uncontrived natural state, then if thought occurs, if emotion erupts, if you will, at that time it is imperative to initially recognize that thought occurrence.

103
00:13:41,943 --> 00:13:48,850
[SPEAKER_00]: When the thought arises, as you read in the second line, one shouldn't stop it, neither should one analyze it.

104
00:13:49,651 --> 00:13:52,954
[SPEAKER_00]: Rather, when the thought arises, one should recognize it.

105
00:13:53,735 --> 00:13:57,499
[SPEAKER_00]: Recognizing the thought then, one should turn one's attention towards its nature.

106
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:03,362
[SPEAKER_00]: And as such, relax or rest then within the empty nature of mind.

107
00:14:03,462 --> 00:14:07,563
[SPEAKER_00]: As such, without stopping or analysing, watch the thought's very nature.

108
00:14:29,241 --> 00:14:39,409
[SPEAKER_00]: So the arising of thought within the experience of resting within the uncontrived nature then, the arising of thought doesn't obscure the absolute nature of mind.

109
00:14:40,950 --> 00:14:42,892
[SPEAKER_00]: By recognizing thought,

110
00:14:44,871 --> 00:15:00,625
[SPEAKER_00]: looking into its nature then, whatever occurs, whatever thought manifests, whatever emotion it might be, recognizing the nature of that thought or emotion then, one should simply relax into its nature and naturally the thought will subside.

111
00:15:01,946 --> 00:15:08,411
[SPEAKER_01]: So, quite often Khense Rinpoche used to give example of throwing stone at the dog.

112
00:15:08,751 --> 00:15:12,373
[SPEAKER_01]: If you throw a stone at a dog, then dog will chase the stone.

113
00:15:13,114 --> 00:15:16,816
[SPEAKER_01]: So when dog chases a stone, you can throw many more stones at the dog.

114
00:15:18,337 --> 00:15:22,440
[SPEAKER_01]: Then if you throw a stone at a lion, the lion will look back at you.

115
00:15:23,741 --> 00:15:25,482
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you cannot throw the second stone.

116
00:15:26,843 --> 00:15:36,909
[SPEAKER_01]: So like that, I think when one thought arises, if you follow the thought, then one thought will chain reaction, lead to another thought, like many, many thoughts.

117
00:15:37,650 --> 00:15:44,074
[SPEAKER_01]: So when the one thought, like one stone to the lion, the lion look back, and then the thought will sort of dissolve, disappear.

118
00:15:46,275 --> 00:15:46,496
[SPEAKER_01]: So.

119
00:15:50,844 --> 00:15:53,665
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't follow thoughts about the past.

120
00:15:54,346 --> 00:15:57,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't anticipate thoughts about the future.

121
00:16:20,424 --> 00:16:22,627
[SPEAKER_00]: directly transcend the external world.

122
00:16:23,768 --> 00:16:25,851
[SPEAKER_00]: That is called the four parts without three.

123
00:16:30,282 --> 00:16:37,985
[SPEAKER_00]: As such, one shouldn't dwell in the past, thinking about things that one has done in whatever form that may take.

124
00:16:38,965 --> 00:16:49,169
[SPEAKER_00]: Similarly then, one shouldn't anticipate the future, thinking about making too many plans and reflecting on what one should or shouldn't do at a particular time in the future, etc.

125
00:16:49,849 --> 00:16:51,550
[SPEAKER_00]: One is advised to avoid these two.

126
00:16:55,452 --> 00:17:02,782
[SPEAKER_01]: In this way, you will be able to get rid of all the negative karma, and you will be able to get rid of all the negative karma.

127
00:17:11,902 --> 00:17:14,824
[SPEAKER_00]: and to then directly transcend the external world.

128
00:17:15,504 --> 00:17:25,751
[SPEAKER_00]: So here when we reflect using the three times, we've spoken about not dwelling in the past and similarly then about anticipating the future.

129
00:17:26,872 --> 00:17:33,336
[SPEAKER_00]: Directly transcending the external world means to not become involved in that which is in front of us at the very moment.

130
00:17:34,714 --> 00:17:35,894
[SPEAKER_00]: in any given time.

131
00:17:35,914 --> 00:17:40,736
[SPEAKER_00]: As such, we think about overcoming the thoughts of the three times.

132
00:17:41,236 --> 00:17:43,697
[SPEAKER_00]: This then is the fourth part without three.

133
00:18:06,142 --> 00:18:13,833
[SPEAKER_00]: If you maintain the recognition of thoughts, you will feel that they do not truly begin, remain or end.

134
00:18:14,875 --> 00:18:18,199
[SPEAKER_00]: Though you notice them, they have no effect on your true nature.

135
00:18:19,321 --> 00:18:22,005
[SPEAKER_00]: That is the bare natural state, the way it is.

136
00:18:23,483 --> 00:18:33,085
[SPEAKER_00]: As such, when we think about the recognition of thoughts, here then, it's essential that we recognize the kind of empty nature of thoughts.

137
00:18:33,205 --> 00:18:39,427
[SPEAKER_00]: As such, really when we look at a thought, it doesn't truly begin or come into existence.

138
00:18:51,892 --> 00:18:54,175
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't do this, you won't be able to do this.

139
00:18:58,597 --> 00:19:08,444
[SPEAKER_00]: So, for example, if we take a crystal and we put it in sunlight, for example, then almost instantaneously rainbow colors will reflect from the stone.

140
00:19:09,645 --> 00:19:18,591
[SPEAKER_00]: Similarly, then, when we think about a mind, when it is put before various objects, etc., it is almost as if instantaneously thoughts arise.

141
00:19:19,132 --> 00:19:23,235
[SPEAKER_00]: However, when the condition for their arisal, in the example of the crystal, the light,

142
00:19:23,935 --> 00:19:29,397
[SPEAKER_00]: is absent, the rainbow-colored light is naturally absent as well.

143
00:19:29,477 --> 00:19:40,300
[SPEAKER_00]: So similarly when the object that gives rise, or the idea to give rise to a continuity of thought is missing, then it is as if the thought was never there.

144
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:44,141
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not an inherent or integral part of the nature of one's mind.

145
00:19:52,239 --> 00:19:57,417
[SPEAKER_01]: DANG PO TZAM NI CHE MA NYONG BA YIN DI KHAO SOG DE NI THAR MA CHE BA JI NGAG BAR BYA MA YIN DUY NGAG PA ME BA.

